# Node tests

## Purpose

Fast, co-located tests for schemas, pagination, and module behavior without requiring Redis.

## Architecture decisions

- `node:test` + `node:assert/strict` only (no Jest/Vitest in this repo).
- Tests live beside source: `examples.test.ts` next to `examples.service.ts`.
- Redis optional — test no-Redis paths by default.

## Required patterns

| Target | Test |
| ------ | ---- |
| Schemas | Defaults, rejection of invalid input |
| Pagination | `paginatedQuerySchema` coerce/default |
| OpenAPI | Key paths registered |
| Services | Behavior with mocked Prisma when needed |

## Good examples

```ts
test("list query schema rejects unsupported sort", () => {
  assert.equal(listExamplesQuerySchema.safeParse({ sort: "id" }).success, false);
});
```

## Bad examples

```ts
import { describe, it, expect } from "vitest";  // wrong runner
test("redis queue", ...) // requires Redis in unit test without opt-in
```

## Explicit prohibitions

- No requiring Redis for default unit tests.
- No e2e framework in `src/**/*.test.ts` unless explicitly added later.

## AI guidance

Add schema/parsing tests for every new list or create endpoint. Run `pnpm verify` before commit.
